        "answer": {
          "short": "For example, $(3,8)$ and $(4,6)$, in dividend–denominator order. Positive whole-number choices are factor pairs of $24$.",
          "worked": "Dividing by $\\frac{1}{n}$ is multiplying by $n$, so the two numbers must have product $24$. For example:\n$$\\begin{align*}3\\div\\frac{1}{8}&=3\\times8\\\\&=24\\\\4\\div\\frac{1}{6}&=4\\times6\\\\&=24\\end{align*}$$",
